Reconstruction

Suppose the original object disappears.

You keep only

R(S).

Then reconstruction becomes

\hat S
=
\arg\min_X
d(R(X),R(S))

Find the representation whose relational signature most closely matches the original.

This is exactly how many recognition problems are posed in machine learning and graph matching: recover the object whose relationships best fit the observed constraints.

